Recursion is a technique where a function calls itself to solve a smaller instance of the same problem. It requires a base case to stop the recursion and a recursive step that reduces the problem. Example (factorial):

def factorial(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return 1
    else:
        return n * factorial(n-1)

SELECT MAX(salary) FROM employees WHERE salary < (SELECT MAX(salary) FROM employees);

Alternatively using LIMIT/OFFSET:
SELECT DISTINCT salary FROM employees ORDER BY salary DESC LIMIT 1 OFFSET 1;
